; Axis A (cross-ref name indexing) — negative direction.
;
; Both `(phrase)` instances omit `:name`, so both materialize the
; same `origin` default. The unused `phrase-name` value-kind only
; exists to mark `phrase` as a cross-ref target (without it,
; `collectCrossRefTargets` returns empty and the registration
; path never runs for `phrase` instances at all). With axis A off
; the pre-pass does not see the defaulted names; the registry
; stays empty and nothing collides. With axis A on, two-time
; registration of `origin` collides at the synthetic default
; path -> `duplicate_cross_ref_target`. The diagnostic carries an
; empty path (`emitDuplicateCrossRef` surfaces on the span only),
; so the harness reports it as `duplicate_cross_ref_target` at `[]`.
;
; `expected.sjon` matches the axis-off baseline (clean).
(plugin :name probe :version "1.0.0"
  (value-kind :name phrase-name
    :underlying symbol
    :cross-ref (cross-ref :target phrase))
  (form :name phrase
    (key :name name :type symbol :default origin :optional false)))

(phrase)
(phrase)
